{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "tr-05-two-trains-opposite-directions",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Two Trains Moving in Opposite Directions",
    "description": "Add relative speeds and add train lengths to solve head-on crossings, unknown lengths, unknown speeds, and initial-gap problems.",
    "teachingApproach": "Establish the sum-speed/sum-length model, reverse it for unknown length or speed, handle equal speeds and initial gaps, move to passenger observations and equal-length pole-time cancellation, then finish with repeated separation.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 30,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 20, Problems on Trains. Approved scope: Teach head-on train crossings as one closing problem: total distance to clear = sum of train lengths, relative speed = sum of speeds. Use this to find crossing time, an unknown length, or an unknown speed. Include equal-speed trains, trains initially separated by a gap, a passenger in one train timing the other, equal-length trains with known pole-crossing times, and the chapter pattern where two trains start a fixed distance apart and the same separation reappears after they cross."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "When two trains approach each other, the picture is wonderfully symmetric: both trains help close the distance, and both train lengths must clear.\n\nAdd the speeds. Add the lengths. Then divide.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "For two trains coming toward each other, two things add at once:\n\nrelative speed = speed₁ + speed₂\ndistance to clear = length₁ + length₂\n\nThey have fully crossed only when both rear ends have cleared each other.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Example: 150 m and 250 m trains at 54 and 90 km/hr.\nRelative speed = 144 km/hr = 40 m/s.\nTotal length = 400 m.\nTime = 400/40 = 10 s.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
