    "teach_5": {
      "id": "teach_5",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "If the trains start with a gap, add that gap to the two train lengths.\n\nA 150 m train and a 100 m train have 100 m of empty track between their nearest ends. To pass completely, the relative motion must cover 150 + 100 + 100 = 350 m.",
